From 33652e4f476115a47b650cedb45742fd6771a494 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 11:57:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Redesign UI: light editorial dossier with blueprint dark mode
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replaces the indigo/glassmorphism cyber theme with a flat "engineer's
dossier" design: Fraunces/Public Sans/JetBrains Mono type system, a
hairline-bordered plate/corner-tick component style, and numbered
exhibit sections. Light (paper/ink) is now the default theme; the
dark toggle becomes a literal blueprint (deep blue, chalk-line type)
instead of a simple color inversion.

- Hero swaps the headshot for an animated RAG-pipeline schematic
  (Framer Motion) and shows the full name, Rayan Erold Tsapi Meguie.
- Projects: numbered catalog grid replaces the horizontal carousel;
  kept the architecture-details modal with each project's real
  technical bullets.
- Contact: replaced the fake, non-functional submit form with direct
  email/phone/location cards plus GitHub/LinkedIn links.
- Playground (AI agent sandbox) and Certificates (copy cert ID,
  signatory) keep their exact working logic — visuals only restyled.
- Fixed a pre-existing bug where the sandbox terminal's auto-scroll
  effect fired on first mount and yanked the whole page down on load.
- Removed unused profile image import and now-unused glass/gradient
  Tailwind utilities in favor of the new flat design tokens.

Verified with `npm run build` and a Playwright pass over light mode,
blueprint dark mode, and mobile width (390px), including the mobile
nav drawer and both agent-sandbox tabs.
